.TH CSL 1.SH NAMEcsl, csl020 \- Microware's C shared library modules.SH DESCRIPTION\fBcsl\fRis Microware's C Shared Library, the run-time module that programs builtwith Ultra C call into instead of carrying the C library themselves;\fBcsl020\fRis the same for the 68020, 68030 and 68040.  They are not programs: aprogram that needs one finds it by name in memory, loading it from theexecution directory the first time.  The programs here that need\fBcsl\fRsay so in\fBDOC/INDEX\fR.\fR.PPThey ship on this disk by Microware's permission, recorded in\fBSOURCES.txt\fR,\fRand your own OS-9 may have newer editions.\fBDOC/README-CIO\fRdescribes the run-time modules and how to use your own..SH SEE ALSOcio, math